{"key":"specroot","result":"{\"id\": \"spec.json\", \"pointer\": \"\", \"view\": \"value\", \"value\": {\"format_version\": 2, \"case_id\": \"wave-map-energy\", \"full_target\": \"Let \\\\(n,m\\\\geq1\\\\) be integers and let\\n\\\\(u:\\\\mathbb R^n\\\\times(0,\\\\infty)\\\\to\\\\mathbb R^m\\\\) be jointly smooth.\\nFix \\\\(q\\\\in\\\\mathbb R^m\\\\) with \\\\(|q|=1\\\\). Assume:\\n\\n1. \\\\(|u(x,t)|=1\\\\) for all \\\\(x\\\\) and \\\\(t>0\\\\).\\n2. The acceleration \\\\(u_{tt}-\\\\Delta_xu\\\\) is normal to the sphere at\\n   \\\\(u\\\\): at each point there is a real scalar \\\\(a(x,t)\\\\) with\\n   \\\\(u_{tt}-\\\\Delta_xu=a u\\\\). No regularity of the selected scalar is\\n   assumed.\\n3. For every \\\\(0<s<t<\\\\infty\\\\), a compact set\\n   \\\\(C_{[s,t]}\\\\subset\\\\mathbb R^n\\\\) exists such that \\\\(u(x,r)=q\\\\) for\\n   \\\\(x\\\\notin C_{[s,t]}\\\\), \\\\(r\\\\in[s,t]\\\\).\\n\\nWith Euclidean norms and Lebesgue measure, define\\n\\n\\\\[\\ne(x,t)=|u_t(x,t)|^2+\\\\sum_{j=1}^n|\\\\partial_{x_j}u(x,t)|^2,\\n\\\\qquad E(t)=\\\\int_{\\\\mathbb R^n}e(x,t)\\\\,dx.\\n\\\\]\\n\\nThe spatial gradient square is the Frobenius square, and\\n\\\\(\\\\Delta_xu=\\\\sum_j\\\\partial_{x_jx_j}u\\\\) component by component.\\nProve integrability of \\\\(e(\\\\cdot,t)\\\\), differentiability of \\\\(E\\\\),\\nand \\\\(E'(t)=0\\\\) for every \\\\(t>0\\\\). No assertion at time zero is required.\", \"conclusion\": \"For every t>0, e(·,t) is absolutely Lebesgue integrable on ℝ^n, E is differentiable at t, and E'(t)=0. In addition E(s)=E(t) for all s,t>0; no assertion at time zero is made.\", \"parameters\": [{\"symbol\": \"n\", \"type\": \"integer\"}, {\"symbol\": \"m\", \"type\": \"integer\"}, {\"symbol\": \"u\", \"type\": \"map ℝ^n × (0,∞) → ℝ^m\"}, {\"symbol\": \"q\", \"type\": \"vector in ℝ^m\"}], \"hypotheses\": [{\"id\": \"H001\", \"statement\": \"n≥1 and m≥1.\", \"origin\": \"problem.md:25\"}, {\"id\": \"H002\", \"statement\": \"u:ℝ^n × (0,∞) → ℝ^m is jointly C^∞ (smooth) on this open domain.\", \"origin\": \"problem.md:25-26\"}, {\"id\": \"H003\", \"statement\": \"|q|=1.\", \"origin\": \"problem.md:27\"}, {\"id\": \"H004\", \"statement\": \"For every x∈ℝ^n and every t>0, |u(x,t)|=1.\", \"origin\": \"problem.md:29\"}, {\"id\": \"H005\", \"statement\": \"For every x∈ℝ^n and every t>0 there exists a real scalar a such that u_tt(x,t)−Δ_xu(x,t)=a u(x,t). No regularity of a selected scalar field is assumed.\", \"origin\": \"problem.md:30-33\"}, {\"id\": \"H006\", \"statement\": \"For every pair of real times 0<s<t<∞ there exists a compact C⊂ℝ^n such that u(x,r)=q for every x∉C and every r∈[s,t].\", \"origin\": \"problem.md:34-36\"}], \"definitions\": [{\"id\": \"D001\", \"symbol\": \"u_t\", \"type\": \"map ℝ^n × (0,∞) → ℝ^m\", \"definition\": \"u_t(x,t)=∂u(x,t)/∂t, the componentwise time derivative.\", \"depends_on\": [], \"requires\": [\"H002\"], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"x\", \"type\": \"point of ℝ^n\"}, {\"symbol\": \"t\", \"type\": \"real in (0,∞)\"}], \"objects\": [\"u\", \"x\", \"t\"]}, {\"id\": \"D002\", \"symbol\": \"u_tt\", \"type\": \"map ℝ^n × (0,∞) → ℝ^m\", \"definition\": \"u_tt(x,t)=∂u_t(x,t)/∂t, the componentwise second time derivative.\", \"depends_on\": [\"D001\"], \"requires\": [\"H002\"], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"x\", \"type\": \"point of ℝ^n\"}, {\"symbol\": \"t\", \"type\": \"real in (0,∞)\"}], \"objects\": [\"u_t\", \"x\", \"t\"]}, {\"id\": \"D003\", \"symbol\": \"D_xu\", \"type\": \"spatial derivative matrix field on ℝ^n × (0,∞)\", \"definition\": \"D_xu has columns ∂_{x_j}u for j=1,...,n, with ∂_{x_j} the componentwise partial derivative in coordinate j; ∂_{x_jx_j}u denotes its second derivative in that coordinate. Derivatives of u_t use the same convention. Its Frobenius square is |D_xu|²=Σ_{j=1}^n|∂_{x_j}u|².\", \"depends_on\": [\"D001\"], \"requires\": [\"H002\"], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"x\", \"type\": \"point of ℝ^n\"}, {\"symbol\": \"t\", \"type\": \"real in (0,∞)\"}, {\"symbol\": \"j\", \"type\": \"index in {1,...,n}\"}], \"objects\": [\"n\", \"m\", \"u\", \"u_t\", \"x\", \"t\", \"j\"]}, {\"id\": \"D004\", \"symbol\": \"Δ_xu\", \"type\": \"map ℝ^n × (0,∞) → ℝ^m\", \"definition\": \"Δ_xu(x,t)=Σ_{j=1}^n ∂_{x_jx_j}u(x,t), component by component.\", \"depends_on\": [\"D003\"], \"requires\": [\"H002\"], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"x\", \"type\": \"point of ℝ^n\"}, {\"symbol\": \"t\", \"type\": \"real in (0,∞)\"}, {\"symbol\": \"j\", \"type\": \"index in {1,...,n}\"}], \"objects\": [\"n\", \"u\", \"D_xu\", \"x\", \"t\", \"j\"]}, {\"id\": \"D005\", \"symbol\": \"e\", \"type\": \"real-valued map on ℝ^n × (0,∞)\", \"definition\": \"e(x,t)=|u_t(x,t)|²+Σ_{j=1}^n|∂_{x_j}u(x,t)|². Norms and dot products throughout are Euclidean; all spatial integrals are Lebesgue integrals, written dx. Write e_t for the time partial derivative of e.\", \"depends_on\": [\"D001\", \"D003\"], \"requires\": [\"H002\"], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"x\", \"type\": \"point of ℝ^n\"}, {\"symbol\": \"t\", \"type\": \"real in (0,∞)\"}, {\"symbol\": \"j\", \"type\": \"index in {1,...,n}\"}], \"objects\": [\"n\", \"m\", \"u\", \"u_t\", \"D_xu\", \"x\", \"t\", \"j\"]}, {\"id\": \"D006\", \"symbol\": \"E\", \"type\": \"real-valued function on (0,∞)\", \"definition\": \"E(t)=∫_{ℝ^n}e(x,t) dx, the finite real Lebesgue integral, with exactly the normalization in the exercise (no factor 1/2).\", \"depends_on\": [\"D005\"], \"requires\": [\"H002\", \"N002\"], \"binders\": [{\"symbol\": \"x\", \"type\": \"point of ℝ^n\"}, {\"symbol\": \"t\", \"type\": \"real in (0,∞)\"}], \"objects\": [\"n\", \"e\", \"x\", \"t\"]}], \"logic\": {\"classical\": true, \"rules\": [\"direct\", \"forall_introduction\", \"exists_elimination\", \"implication_introduction\"], \"calculations\": [\"equality\", \"definitions\", \"finite_algebra\", \"finite_order\", \"finite_sums\"], \"primitives\": [{\"symbol\": \"0\", \"type\": \"typed numeral\", \"meaning\": \"Zero of the explicitly specified mathematical type.\"}, {\"sy