D003:make("Spatial derivative matrix has n columns in ℝ^m, with first and second coordinate derivatives and derivatives of u_t explicitly defined. Frobenius square equals the stated finite sum by the norm convention. Dependence on D001 and H002 is legitimate and guarded at each R use.",["spec.json#/definitions/2","problem.md:38-46","global-overview.json#/inference_edges"]),
D004:make("Componentwise Laplacian is the finite sum of the n pure second spatial derivatives, with the original sign convention and domain. D003 and H002 provide the required notation and existence; no wave-map equation is hidden in this definition.",["spec.json#/definitions/3","spec.json#/definitions/2","problem.md:45-46","global-overview.json#/inference_edges"]),
D005:make("The real density is exactly |u_t|²+Σ_j|∂_ju|² with Euclidean norms/dot products and Lebesgue spatial integration. e_t denotes its time partial derivative; joint smoothness under H002 ensures it exists through ordinary finite differentiation. No support, integrability or derivative formula is postulated by the definition.",["spec.json#/definitions/4","spec.json#/hypotheses/1","problem.md:38-46","global-overview.json#/inference_edges"]),
